<crash-analysis>
The crash is a memory leak caused by a bug in the `tidy-html5` project.

**Analysis:**
The `CleanSpaces` function in `/src/tidy-html5/src/parser.c` allocates a `Stack` object using `TY_(newStack)` at line 555. However, this allocated stack is never freed before the function returns. This leads to a memory leak every time `CleanSpaces` is called. The LeakSanitizer detects this accumulation of unfreed memory, resulting in the reported crash.

**Suggestion:**
Add a call to `TY_(freeStack)(stack);` at the end of the `CleanSpaces` function, before it returns, to release the allocated memory.

```c
static void CleanSpaces(TidyDocImpl* doc, Node* node)
{
Stack *stack = TY_(newStack)(doc, 16);
Node *next;

while (node)
{
// ... existing code ...
}

TY_(freeStack)(stack); // Add this line
}
```
</crash-analysis>

